      "message": "[warning] Line 1074: 🟡 Retransmission pacing sleeps synchronously inside `readCallback`. At the 64-packet cap and a low configured bitrate, handling one NACK can occupy the receive loop for seconds, preventing RTP/RTCP from being drained and causing further socket-buffer loss. Queue retransmissions to a sender/pacer worker or make this scheduling nonblocking instead of sleeping in the read path.",
